{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01004",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.1,
      "end_seconds": 2.89,
      "duration_seconds": 1.79,
      "text": "Good afternoon, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 3.42,
      "end_seconds": 9.36,
      "duration_seconds": 5.94,
      "text": "So, you're alright, take a seat. What can I do for you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 10.15,
      "end_seconds": 17.7,
      "duration_seconds": 7.55,
      "text": "Uh, you know, hello, doctor, I came in with them, if that's okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 18.21,
      "end_seconds": 25.01,
      "duration_seconds": 6.8,
      "text": "Doctor, it's a red warm patch on my shin. That's what we're worried about."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 26.86,
      "end_seconds": 30.51,
      "duration_seconds": 3.65,
      "text": "How many days or weeks has it been?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 31.86,
      "end_seconds": 36.9,
      "duration_seconds": 5.04,
      "text": "I mean, it's been about a month, I'm fairly sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 38.65,
      "end_seconds": 41.05,
      "duration_seconds": 2.4,
      "text": "How much does it limit you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 42.46,
      "end_seconds": 46.02,
      "duration_seconds": 3.56,
      "text": "Um, it feels moderate to me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 47.26,
      "end_seconds": 49.76,
      "duration_seconds": 2.5,
      "text": "Alright, any other symptoms with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 51.18,
      "end_seconds": 57.7,
      "duration_seconds": 6.52,
      "text": "Erm, when it starts I tend to get a sore leg as well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 58.34,
      "end_seconds": 64.91,
      "duration_seconds": 6.57,
      "text": "And the other thing I wanted to mention is that I can't really—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 65.01,
      "end_seconds": 70.89,
      "duration_seconds": 5.88,
      "text": "Tell the doctor about the other thing, that's what worries me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 72.49,
      "end_seconds": 80.62,
      "duration_seconds": 8.13,
      "text": "I, I was getting to that! The sore leg? That's been for about four days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 81.83,
      "end_seconds": 90.79,
      "duration_seconds": 8.96,
      "text": "Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 94.23,
      "end_seconds": 98.48,
      "duration_seconds": 4.25,
      "text": "I notice it more with walking. It's moderate, honestly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_5",
      "role": "UNKNOWN",
      "start_seconds": 100.03,
      "end_seconds": 102.74,
      "duration_seconds": 2.71,
      "text": "Mm, that's what happened, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 104.37,
      "end_seconds": 107.59,
      "duration_seconds": 3.22,
      "text": "And what about cut or rash elsewhere?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 111.42,
      "end_seconds": 122.23,
      "duration_seconds": 10.81,
      "text": "No, no cut, no rash elsewhere. I was feeling shivery at one point, but that went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 126.81,
      "end_seconds": 128.38,
      "duration_seconds": 1.57,
      "text": "Any shortness of breath?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 128.9,
      "end_seconds": 131.22,
      "duration_seconds": 2.32,
      "text": "No. No shortness of breath."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 131.65,
      "end_seconds": 134.46,
      "duration_seconds": 2.81,
      "text": "Understood. Any breathing difficulties apart from this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 138.96,
      "end_seconds": 140.82,
      "duration_seconds": 1.86,
      "text": "No problems with breathing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 142.16,
      "end_seconds": 145.31,
      "duration_seconds": 3.15,
      "text": "What line of work are you in?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 146.42,
      "end_seconds": 151.09,
      "duration_seconds": 4.67,
      "text": "I'm a bus driver, so I sit for long hours."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 152.98,
      "end_seconds": 156.86,
      "duration_seconds": 3.88,
      "text": "What does a normal day of food look like?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 158.12,
      "end_seconds": 161.69,
      "duration_seconds": 3.57,
      "text": "Lots of rice, lentils and some fruit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 163.09,
      "end_seconds": 165.88,
      "duration_seconds": 2.79,
      "text": "Any past operations I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 167.43,
      "end_seconds": 171.43,
      "duration_seconds": 4.0,
      "text": "Just my septum straightened, in my thirties."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 172.41,
      "end_seconds": 175.8,
      "duration_seconds": 3.39,
      "text": "Okay, before we go further, any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 177.25,
      "end_seconds": 181.51,
      "duration_seconds": 4.26,
      "text": "Actually, no, nothing as far as I know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 182.97,
      "end_seconds": 190.98,
      "duration_seconds": 8.01,
      "text": "Actually, I remember she had some kind of reaction to amoxicillin before. I couldn't swear to it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 192.09,
      "end_seconds": 195.18,
      "duration_seconds": 3.09,
      "text": "Maybe, but I don't recall it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 195.78,
      "end_seconds": 200.35,
      "duration_seconds": 4.57,
      "text": "Alright, so that's unclear. I'll record what each of you said."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 218.15,
      "end_seconds": 222.28,
      "duration_seconds": 4.13,
      "text": "Are you taking anything regularly, including from the pharmacy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 222.8,
      "end_seconds": 232.93,
      "duration_seconds": 10.13,
      "text": "Iron tablets, once a day. Hydrocortisone cream. I take it when needed. Gliclazide. I take it 80 milligrams, twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 233.84,
      "end_seconds": 245.73,
      "duration_seconds": 11.89,
      "text": "Actually, you know, doctor, I think the last prescription for the gliclazide was 40 milligrams. We changed it at the last visit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 247.04,
      "end_seconds": 251.17,
      "duration_seconds": 4.13,
      "text": "Right, I see. Is the most recent prescription on you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 252.79,
      "end_seconds": 256.16,
      "duration_seconds": 3.37,
      "text": "No, I left it at home."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 258.03,
      "end_seconds": 262.8,
      "duration_seconds": 4.77,
      "text": "What conditions have you been treated for in the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 264.43,
      "end_seconds": 270.35,
      "duration_seconds": 5.92,
      "text": "Ah, I've got low haemoglobin. I've never really been one for hospitals."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 274.62,
      "end_seconds": 275.94,
      "duration_seconds": 1.32,
      "text": "Okay, what else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 277.51,
      "end_seconds": 279.05,
      "duration_seconds": 1.54,
      "text": "I have eczema."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 280.43,
      "end_seconds": 281.13,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Ah."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 284.05,
      "end_seconds": 289.19,
      "duration_seconds": 5.14,
      "text": "Ah, I've had an underactive thyroid, yes. I have diabetes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 290.41,
      "end_seconds": 295.99,
      "duration_seconds": 5.58,
      "text": "Yes, low haemoglobin is known to us, good to have that clear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 303.0,
      "end_seconds": 307.9,
      "duration_seconds": 4.9,
      "text": "Any inherited conditions that you know of in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 309.46,
      "end_seconds": 315.21,
      "duration_seconds": 5.75,
      "text": "Okay, so my aunt has rheumatoid arthritis. Ah, my brother has epilepsy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_6",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 317.1,
      "end_seconds": 332.3,
      "duration_seconds": 15.2,
      "text": "Here are the numbers, doctor. Temp 38.6 degrees, oxygen saturation is 96 percent. BMI works out to 32.5, height 155 centimetres, weight 78 kilos, respiratory rate 18, pressure 110 over 66, pulse 101."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 336.73,
      "end_seconds": 337.75,
      "duration_seconds": 1.02,
      "text": "Okay, noted."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 339.95,
      "end_seconds": 344.19,
      "duration_seconds": 4.24,
      "text": "Let me look at the area, I'll be gentle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 346.11,
      "end_seconds": 347.4,
      "duration_seconds": 1.29,
      "text": "Look straight ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 358.46,
      "end_seconds": 366.56,
      "duration_seconds": 8.1,
      "text": "The shin is red, warm and tender with a clear edge, and I've marked it with a pen."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 371.39,
      "end_seconds": 392.86,
      "duration_seconds": 21.47,
      "text": "Please sit back down. Okay, so my impression is this: The most likely explanation is cellulitis of the leg. We shouldn't forget a blood clot in the leg. Just to be sure I understood. You've had a red warm patch on your shin for about a month, moderate, and no rash elsewhere or cut."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 394.3,
      "end_seconds": 396.53,
      "duration_seconds": 2.23,
      "text": "Yes, you've got it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 398.51,
      "end_seconds": 423.25,
      "duration_seconds": 24.74,
      "text": "Blood tests is what I'd like next, for cellulitis. The result will help us decide whether anything more is needed. Keep the leg raised and come back if the redness goes past the pen line. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 424.79,
      "end_seconds": 426.47,
      "duration_seconds": 1.68,
      "text": "Alright, I follow."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 428.54,
      "end_seconds": 439.77,
      "duration_seconds": 11.23,
      "text": "The thing that would worry me is if the symptoms get worse. If that happens, go to emergency. I'd like you back in two days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 441.78,
      "end_seconds": 444.03,
      "duration_seconds": 2.25,
      "text": "Alright, I'll be back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 445.22,
      "end_seconds": 449.13,
      "duration_seconds": 3.91,
      "text": "What are the next steps as you understand them?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 449.91,
      "end_seconds": 455.37,
      "duration_seconds": 5.46,
      "text": "So, I come back in two days. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 457.45,
      "end_seconds": 463.35,
      "duration_seconds": 5.9,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. Right, that's the plan. Do you want to ask me anything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0062",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 464.7,
      "end_seconds": 466.73,
      "duration_seconds": 2.03,
      "text": "Thank you, doctor, goodbye."
    }
  ]
}